                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h2] Welcome to 3D Hardcore Cube [/h2]\nA game with very noticeable bugs. There’s no way the game was intentionally designed like this, it’s just terribly broken. The only reason I bought this game was for the 1596 total achievements.\nThis is one of the few games where I said to myself, “I’m glad there are only 12 levels, because I don’t want to play more.” You said the game is “difficult” well no sh*t, because the game is awfully made.\nAlso it does not worth the original price, only pay if its on big sale.\n[hr] [/hr] [h3] Broken list and flaws: [/h3] [olist]\n[*] Camera: The camera placement is bad and you made it too complex for no reason. Why not just place it in the middle of the screen and let it follow the player normally?\n[*] Movement: For a platforming game, I expect the movement to at least feel smooth, but no—the movement sucks because of the broken physics.\n[*] Jumping: Sometimes it jumps higher and farther; sometimes it decides to become limp and barely work.\n[*] Jump booster floor: Combined with the already broken jumping, this mechanic makes the game even more broken than it already is.\n[*] Sticky walls: You already have falling floors that disappear after a limited amount of time and do not respawn. Then I jump on it and ended up getting stuck on the side while they fall just because I touched them.\n[*] Level 7: You didn’t teach the player how to duck to progress.\n[*] Level 10: You can easily get stuck in the falling floor. At least playtest your own game to find that out.\n[*] Level 12: Sometimes the bullets shot from the turret hit the spike objects and get redirected, resulting in the player dying because of the sh*tty design.\n[*] The game’s selling point is supposedly the difficulty and soundtrack, but both of them suck.\n[/olist]\n[b]This is my genuine review if I judge it purely as a game. As an achievement hunter, it’s only good because of the total amount of achievements.[/b]",
